                    insight_won:            `Co-created transformation: you diagnosed the real need, put Veridian's own people in the design room, allocated 70-20-10 for behaviour change, aligned three sponsors on one scorecard, stayed inside €840k above the 22% hurdle, and built 3/6/9-month measurement. This is the mandate won the right way.`,
                    insight_rented:         `Strong design, but rented not owned. Your architecture may deliver impact, yet without genuine co-creation Veridian's people didn't help build it — when you leave, the change leaves with you, and the consultancy's “why pay the premium?” lands.`,
                    insight_budget:         `You lost to the budget. Either you breached the €840k cap the CFO claws back, or your margin fell below the 22% approval hurdle. A brilliant design that doesn't clear the gate never gets funded.`,
                    insight_short:          `You fell short of a credible transformation outcome. Re-examine where you order-took the brief, under-co-created, or unbalanced the sponsors — the impact above Level 1 isn't there yet.`,
                    insight_lowimpact:      `Transformation impact stayed low: you bought satisfaction or completion, not behaviour and business change. The 70-20-10 “70” — real applied work — is what moves the needle the CHRO and COO are buying.`,
                    insight_lowalign:       `Sponsor alignment stayed low: you served one sponsor and left the other two without an answer. The balanced scorecard is the artefact that makes all three back the same programme.`,
                    insight_lowcocreate:    `Co-creation stayed low: this reads as your academy that Veridian paid for, not theirs. That is exactly the €1.6M “designed for, not with” failure — and it's why the cheaper bid is tempting.`,
                    insight_lost:           `You signed too late and Veridian defaulted to the consultancy. Speed-to-trust is part of the design: a brilliant proposal delivered after the decision wins nothing.`,
                    insight_renew:          `This is a relationship, not a transaction: measured impact, aligned sponsors and genuine co-creation give you the FY27 renewal and the reference logo Atelier Cadence staked its reputation on.`,

                    hint_budget:            `You've breached the €840k cap or dropped below the 22% margin hurdle. The CFO claws back overruns — cut the lowest-impact formats and protect the on-the-job application that buys behaviour change.`,
                    hint_cocreate:          `Co-creation is dangerously low — this still looks like your academy, not Veridian's. Put their SMEs in the design room and their leaders into delivery, or you can't justify the premium over the cheaper bid.`,
                    hint_align:             `Sponsor alignment is low — you're serving one sponsor and losing the others. Build one balanced scorecard the CHRO, COO and CFO can all sign.`,
                    hint_impact:            `Transformation impact is behind with little time left. Shift toward 70-20-10 applied work and measured behaviour change — satisfaction and completion won't carry the FY27 decision.`,
                    hint_strong:            `Strong position — impact, alignment and co-creation all healthy. Now lock in 3/6/9-month measurement and the renewal logic so it survives to the FY27 funding decision.`,

